A||N||5||86SEFIERO||running stereo amp wires||||1||
Z||000000||86SEFIERO||06-15-2000||03:47 PM||||<BR>I have my amp installed in the rear trunk compartment of my fiero. I need opinions if you think it would be allright to run my wires through the hole where the shift cables enter the firewall. I have triple shielded stinger patch cords do you think that this will pick up engine noise runnng this close to the engine?  I really dont want to drill more holes.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula||06-15-2000||05:59 PM||||I drilled a hole above my ecm and it doesnt make any electrical interference. Of course its just my power wire (10gauge) and Ground Wire (10 gauge).  Rca's and speaker wire might be a different story.<P>btw....... why did you choose the trunk instead of behind the passenger seat?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-16-2000||03:02 AM||||Don't run your low level RCA cables anywhere near the ECM. You will pick up lots of noise!<BR>Power is OK. You can run the RCA's down the passenger side of the engine compartment then drill a hole in the Firewall just under the battery case. Don't run them on the driverside or else you'll end up with "audible" turn signals (A quite "thump" each time the lights flash) Usually behind the seat or under the spare tire are the better locations.||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SEFIERO||06-16-2000||03:27 AM||||I chose the trunk because I am installing two tens one behind each seat. I didn't want to put it up front because it will probably get wet.Thanks for info guys!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||wxxo||06-16-2000||09:00 AM||||im planning on putting in two mtx terminator 12'' speakers behind the seat but im wondering how to cut the firewall because you only get one chance at it. any ideas??||||reg||1
Z||000005||Loki||06-16-2000||09:58 AM||||HEy...<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.cox-internet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cox-internet.com</A> <P>I cut into the "double firewall" easy enough but be carefull, fuel lines run in the drivers side. As for wire running. My first install I ran both power and rca wires through a hole above the ecm. No problems at all. Just remember this, if noise comes through it can be power OR rca.<BR>   Im in the process of redoing my site so if you have any questions ask away....<P>Loki||||reg||1
